<title>USA: House panel blocks plan to fund NEA with SPR oil.</title>
<headline>House panel blocks plan to fund NEA with SPR oil.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. House Appropriations committee defeated an amendment Thursday to sell $89 million worth of oil from the Strategic Petroleum Reserve in the 1998 fiscal year to fund the National Endowment for the Arts.</p>
<p>The amendment failed by a vote of 28 to 31, although three Republicans voted with the Democrats to keep the NEA alive in 1998. The amendment was part of a $13 billion spending bill for energy and lands programs.</p>
<p>The bill still includes a $209 million oil sale that would cover the costs of operating the SPR in 1998. The committee is expected to vote on the entire bill later on Thursday.</p>
<p>((Washington energy desk, 202 898 8467))</p>
